NAME
====

**wattle-gum** - copy Gum modules into a project

SYNOPSIS
========

**wattle gum** [**-d** _directory_ | **--dir** _directory_]
               [**-f** | **--force**] [_module_ ...]

DESCRIPTION
===========

Copy Gum modules into a project. Gum is the set of optional Wattle modules
installed in ``share/wattle/src/gum`` under ``*prefix*``. **g** is a synonym
for ***gum***.

With no _module_, ***gum*** prints the name and a description of each module in
two columns, wrapped as **--help** wraps. With one or more, it copies the files
of each, which are its source and its licence, into the ``gum`` directory of
_directory_, and prints ``copied`` or ``unchanged`` and the path of each file.
A project imports a copy by its path, as in
``(import ./deps/gum/args :as args)``. A build made without the OS library
does not include ***gum***, and it exits with status 1 after saying so.

***gum*** checks every _module_ and every destination before it copies a file.
It exits with status 1 having copied nothing if a _module_ is not one of
Gum's, or if a destination file exists with content that differs from its
source. A file with the same content is left as it is.

OPTIONS
=======

- **-d**, **--dir** _directory_:
  Copy into ``gum`` under _directory_. The default is ``deps``.

- **-f**, **--force**:
  Replace a destination file that differs from its source.

SEE ALSO
========

`wattle(1)`
